# Rebase safety: binding a second provisional job to an already bound WorkId is
# refused (visible standalone, both instances keep their ids); the same call id
# in another session is a different provisional key.
# Observed renames (adapter contract rule 4): the move call is its own Mutate
# activity keyed by the old path, so it seals the read burst of old.rs and opens
# a loop; the rebase is a pure binding (no call id) that moves that loop to
# new.rs (same projection, old path as alias). Moving other.rs onto new.rs
# replaces new.rs: its loop is sealed and the rebind is refused, never merged.
# Renaming a file this turn never touched is a plain standalone.
